#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""firmable — unofficial CLI over the Firmable REST API.

Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Firmable.

Firmable is the AU/NZ B2B sales-intelligence database (~1.5M companies, ~10M
people) carrying ABN/ACN/NZBN, ANZSIC, technographics, work emails and mobiles.
This CLI covers every documented operation in the OpenAPI spec sitting next to
this script (openapi.json, from docs.firmable.com), and adds batch commands that
run a CSV through those endpoints with rate limiting, retries and resume.

Set FIRMABLE_API_KEY in your environment. JSON is written to stdout.

Quick start:
  export FIRMABLE_API_KEY=fbl_...
  ./firmable commands                         # list every available command
  ./firmable help company                     # show args/flags for one command
  ./firmable company --fqdn smec.com
  ./firmable company --abn 47065475149 --csv smec.csv
  ./firmable people --ln-url https://www.linkedin.com/in/some-slug/
  ./firmable people-search --company-id f000000147616 --seniority C-Suite --all
  ./firmable company-batch domains.csv --by fqdn --csv enriched.csv
  ./firmable people-batch profiles.csv --by ln_url --csv contacts.csv
  ./firmable roster companies.csv --column id --enrich --csv people.csv

Auth: a bearer token in the Authorization header. Create the key at
app.firmable.com -> Profile -> Integrations -> API. Keys start with `fbl_`.

Rate limit: 50 requests/second per API key. Batch commands default to 20 rps
across 8 worker threads; raise with --rps / --concurrency at your own risk.

Credits: every successful lookup consumes Firmable credits. Batch commands
resume from their JSONL output by default, so a re-run never re-buys a row you
already have — pass --force to override. --dry-run prints the request without
sending it.

Where the spec lies (handled here, so you don't have to):
  * A lookup miss returns HTTP 500 {"error":"Company profile not found"}, not a
    404. Misses are recorded as misses and never retried.
  * POST /people/search 307-redirects to an internal URL; the redirect must be
    replayed with the method and body intact.
  * /people/search returns {"records":[...],"total":N}, not the bare array the
    spec documents. --all pages on `total`.

Global flags:
  --version, -V    show CLI version
  --help, -h       show this help
"""
